From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:09:46 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 153/154] arm64: dts: exynos9810: gtactive3: split into common
 and per-variant files

The Galaxy Tab Active3 is one board in two variants: the Wi-Fi SM-T570
(gtactive3wifi) and the LTE SM-T575/T575N (gtactive3), which adds the
SoC's own modem. Move everything into exynos9810-gtactive3-common.dtsi
and keep only the identity in the board files, so both variants get
every fix.

exynos9810-gtactive3wifi.dts preprocesses to the same tree as before
(model and compatible move to the end of the root node).

exynos9810-gtactive3.dts is a bring-up board for the LTE variant, from
the stock T575XXSFEYI1 tree of a hw_rev 5 unit: the CP shared memory
and log carveouts are reserved (no-map), the RT5510 that hw_rev 5 does
not fit is disabled, a disabled TAS2562 node marks the real amplifier,
and the sound card stays off until the speaker link points at it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
